          </h2>

          <div class="faq-list">
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Sprout Living third-party tested?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Sprout Living says yes. Every Epic Protein bag states it is third-party tested, every ingredient and batch, and the brand says it spot-tests for arsenic, lead, cadmium and mercury. It does not publish certificates of analysis, and we found no Sprout Living product on the NSF Certified for Sport or Informed Sport databases. Tested athletes should choose a certified product instead.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Sprout Living Epic Protein healthy and clean?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  For most healthy adults, yes. Epic is USDA Organic and Certified Vegan, with no gums, natural flavors or sugar alcohols. Original has six ingredients, 26 g of protein and no added sugar per the label. Flavored bags add 4 g of coconut sugar and stevia leaf. Watch the 310 to 380 mg of sodium per serving if you limit salt.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Does Sprout Living protein contain heavy metals?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Like all plant proteins, it will contain trace heavy metals from soil. Sprout Living says its products consistently test within limits but does not publish the numbers, so the amount per serving is unknown. Choosing Original or Vanilla Lucuma over Chocolate Maca avoids cacao, which tends to raise cadmium and lead readings across the category.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Does Sprout Living contain stevia or sugar?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Original and the unflavored Simple Protein bags contain no sweetener at all. Vanilla Lucuma and Chocolate Maca contain organic coconut sugar, adding 4 g of sugar per serving, plus organic stevia leaf. Real Sport has no added sugar and is sweetened with stevia leaf and banana. No Epic flavor uses erythritol or other sugar alcohols.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Which Sprout Living flavor is best?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  In buyer reviews, Chocolate Maca and Vanilla Lucuma are the most praised flavors, with several buyers saying Chocolate Maca is less gritty than other plant proteins. Original is the best value and the most versatile in cooking, but buyers describe it as plain and earthy in water. We have not tasted them; this is buyer feedback only.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>What are common complaints about Sprout Living?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  The most common complaints in buyer reviews are price and taste: some find Original too earthy on its own, and some feel 20 g of protein in a 38 g flavored scoop is poor value. One reviewer described a chalky, earthy texture. Overall ratings on the brand site and at retailers are high, around 4.8 to 4.9 out of 5.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Sprout Living worth the money?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Epic Original is, if you value an organic, six-ingredient label; it costs about $2.80 per 25 g of protein, or about $2.38 with subscribe and save. The flavored bags at $3.64 per 25 g are harder to justify unless you specifically want a gum-free, natural-flavor-free superfood blend. Orgain and Sunwarrior cost less per gram.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

